[x] Publish the grammar 0.10.0 to crates.io =publish-grammar $Decided with the human 2026-10-05: the CLI ships as prebuilt binaries installable with cargo binstall, and binstall reads the crate from crates.io, which refuses a published crate with a git dependency. crates.io has tree-sitter-actions 0.9.4; Core and the CLI pin 0.10.0 by git rev. Publish 0.10.0 (cargo package --list first: the generated parser and bindings, nothing the build does not need), then depend on it by version in both crates. Open: how the pinned platform composition keeps building against the grammar submodule once the dependency is a registry version; a \[patch.crates-io] in the composition is the usual answer. DONE 2026-10-05: 0.10.0 is on crates.io (tag v0.10.0); the crate now ships the MIT license and not node_modules' licenses, as 0.9.4 did. Decided with the human (option A): Core takes the published grammar in every checkout, as a consumer does, so the platform .cargo/config.toml patch to the submodule is gone. That patch had also made Core's committed lockfile name a local path, failing --locked in Core's CI for at least its last 100 runs. validate-pinned proves the published grammar Core resolves is the submodule, file for file; an unpublished grammar change uses a one-invocation --config override (Core's README). Core's --no-default-features tests that format .actions are now gated on the formatting feature.$ !2 ^2026-10-05T19:31 %2026-10-05T20:14 #01a10f0d-78f9-7235-8c70-651a9144080c
